pySMESH: MaxElementArea bounds the triangles of MEFISTO_2D, and a bound the boundary cannot
meet is reported (SMESH V9_9_0 MEFISTO carried forward; applies after mefisto.patch).

Defect: MaxElementArea had no effect on MEFISTO_2D below the size of the boundary segments,
and a looser bound could give a finer mesh than a tighter one. The compute reported success
either way.

Symptom: the 4 x 4 square with 8 segments per side (boundary edges 0.5). max_area 4, 1 and
0.0625 all gave the same 134 triangles; with 0.0625 the largest has area 0.176, 2.8 times
the bound, and 134 is below the 16 / 0.0625 = 256 the bound needs. max_area 0.25 gave 96
triangles, fewer than max_area 1. A 3 x 7 x 11 box with LocalLength(1.0): MaxElementArea(1.0)
gave 440 triangles, the largest of area 1.77, with 0.187 degree slivers, while
MaxElementArea(4.0) and no 2-D hypothesis gave 1136 triangles, the largest of area 0.573.

Root cause, measured with an instrumented build: StdMeshers_MEFISTO_2D turns max_area A into
the edge bound aretmx = 1.5 sqrt(2 A / sqrt 3) (StdMeshers_MEFISTO_2D.cxx:170, :248), and
aptrte clamps it (extern/mefisto2/aptrte.cxx:346-354) before it stores it for areteideale
(:357), which sizes every vertex of the triangulation (tehote, trte.c:2105):
* a bound below the shortest boundary edge goes back up to that edge, and below half of it,
  on an uneven boundary, to (aremin + 2 aremax) / 3, so a tighter bound has no effect;
* a bound over 2.05 x the longest boundary edge goes down to that edge, while one just below
  2.05 x is kept, so the interior grew coarser than the boundary for 1.0 x .. 2.05 x and
  fell back to the boundary size above it.
Two other suspects change no mesh (identical meshes in an instrumented build): the line of
mefisto.patch that sets mnpxyd[ns1].z for mnpxyd[ns].z (aptrte.cxx:305 after that patch),
and the boundary loop reading aretemaxface_ before :357 sets it for this face. Both only
touch the vertex sizes in mnpxyd, which tehote sets again from areteideale for nutysu = 1,
the value MEFISTO_2D passes.

Change:
* aptrte.h, aptrte.cxx: aptrte takes a trailing aretmxIsBound (default false). When it is
  true, the three clamps become aretmx = Min( aretmx, aremax ): the bound refines the face
  below the boundary edges where it asks for that, and never coarsens it past the longest
  boundary edge.
* StdMeshers_MEFISTO_2D.cxx: passes aretmxIsBound when MaxElementArea applies. After the
  triangles are stored, a face whose largest triangle exceeds max_area (relative 1e-9) gets a
  COMPERR_WARNING that names both areas. That happens where the boundary edges are too long
  for the bound.

Not changed: a face with no 2-D hypothesis or with LengthFromEdges keeps the clamps. There
aretmx is the mean 3-D boundary edge, and on a curved face aremin and aremax are measured on
the scaled UV boundary, so the clamps do act and shape those meshes (a radius-4 sphere with
24 segments: 1816 triangles with the clamps, 7112 with the bound). Every other algorithm.
diff --git a/src/MEFISTO2/aptrte.cxx b/src/MEFISTO2/aptrte.cxx
--- a/src/MEFISTO2/aptrte.cxx
+++ b/src/MEFISTO2/aptrte.cxx
@@ -91,7 +91,8 @@
               Z   nbpti,  R2 *   uvpti,
               Z & nbst,   R2 * & uvst,
               Z & nbt,    Z  * & nust,
-              Z & ierr )
+              Z & ierr,
+              bool aretmxIsBound )
 //+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 // but : appel de la triangulation par un arbre-4 recouvrant
 // ----- de triangles equilateraux
@@ -346,6 +347,18 @@
 //debut ajout  9/11/2006  ................................................
   // devenu un commentaire aretmx = Min( aretmx, aremax ); //pour homogeneiser
 
+  if ( aretmxIsBound )
+  {
+    // pySMESH: aretmx comes from MaxElementArea, a bound. It refines the face below the
+    // boundary edges where it asks for that, and it never coarsens the face past the
+    // longest boundary edge. The clamps below raised a bound under the shortest
+    // boundary edge back to that edge, so MaxElementArea had no effect there, and set
+    // a bound over 2.05 x the longest edge to that edge, so a looser bound could give a
+    // finer mesh than a tighter one. Sizing from the boundary keeps them.
+    aretmx = Min( aretmx, aremax );
+  }
+  else
+  {
   // protection contre une arete max desiree trop grande ou trop petite
   if( aretmx > aremax*2.05 ) aretmx = aremax;
 
@@ -355,6 +368,7 @@
 
   if( aretmx < aremin  && aremin > 0 )
     aretmx = aremin;
+  }
 
   //sauvegarde pour la fonction areteideale_
   aretemaxface_ = aretmx;
diff --git a/src/MEFISTO2/aptrte.h b/src/MEFISTO2/aptrte.h
--- a/src/MEFISTO2/aptrte.h
+++ b/src/MEFISTO2/aptrte.h
@@ -63,7 +63,8 @@
               Z nblf,   Z *nudslf, R2 *uvslf,
               Z nbpti,  R2 *uvpti,
               Z & nbst, R2 * & uvst, Z & nbt, Z * & nust,
-              Z & ierr );
+              Z & ierr,
+              bool aretmxIsBound = false ); // pySMESH: aretmx comes from MaxElementArea
 //+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 // but : appel de la triangulation par un arbre-4 recouvrant
 // ----- de triangles equilateraux
diff --git a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_MEFISTO_2D.cxx b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_MEFISTO_2D.cxx
--- a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_MEFISTO_2D.cxx
+++ b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_MEFISTO_2D.cxx
@@ -276,12 +276,33 @@
   {
     // Compute
     aptrte(nutysu, aretmx,
-           nblf, nudslf, uvslf, nbpti, uvpti, nbst, uvst, nbt, nust, ierr);
+           nblf, nudslf, uvslf, nbpti, uvpti, nbst, uvst, nbt, nust, ierr,
+           /*aretmxIsBound=*/_hypMaxElementArea != NULL); // pySMESH
 
     if (ierr == 0)
     {
       StoreResult(nbst, uvst, nbt, nust, mefistoToDS, scalex, scaley);
       isOk = true;
+
+      // pySMESH: MaxElementArea bounds the triangle area. Along boundary edges too long
+      // for the bound the triangles stay larger; report that instead of returning a
+      // mesh that breaks the bound with no word.
+      if ( _hypMaxElementArea )
+      {
+        double maxArea = 0;
+        if ( SMESHDS_SubMesh* sm = aMesh.GetMeshDS()->MeshElements( F ))
+          for ( SMDS_ElemIteratorPtr fIt = sm->GetElements(); fIt->more(); )
+          {
+            const SMDS_MeshElement* f = fIt->next();
+            SMESH_NodeXYZ p0( f->GetNode( 0 )), p1( f->GetNode( 1 )), p2( f->GetNode( 2 ));
+            const double area = 0.5 * (( p1 - p0 ) ^ ( p2 - p0 )).Modulus();
+            maxArea = area > maxArea ? area : maxArea;
+          }
+        if ( maxArea > _maxElementArea * ( 1. + 1e-9 ))
+          error( COMPERR_WARNING, SMESH_Comment( "MaxElementArea " ) << _maxElementArea
+                 << " is not met: the largest triangle has area " << maxArea
+                 << "; the boundary edges are too long for this bound" );
+      }
     }
     else
     {
